sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant APIServer as API Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Processor as Processor<br/>(Sync Mode)
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>6379/TCP
    participant AsyncProc as Async Processor<br/>(Async Mode)
    participant InfGW as Inference Gateway<br/>(llm-d GIE/EPP)
    participant Operator as Operator
    participant KubeAPI as kube-apiserver<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Client,InfGW: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission (Sync Mode)
        Client->>APIServer: POST /v1/batches<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, Authorization header
        APIServer->>PG: Store job state<br/>5432/TCP, credentials
        APIServer->>S3: Store input files<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, AWS IAM
        Processor->>PG: Poll pending jobs<br/>5432/TCP, credentials
        Processor->>InfGW: Dispatch inference requests<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, Bearer token
        InfGW-->>Processor: Inference response
        Processor->>S3: Store output files<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, AWS IAM
        Processor->>PG: Update job status<br/>5432/TCP, credentials
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over Client,AsyncProc: Flow 2: Batch Job Submission (Async Mode)
        Client->>APIServer: POST /v1/batches<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, Authorization header
        APIServer->>PG: Store job state<br/>5432/TCP, credentials
        Processor->>Redis: Enqueue to sorted-set<br/>6379/TCP, credentials
        AsyncProc->>Redis: Poll queue<br/>6379/TCP, configurable TLS
        AsyncProc->>InfGW: Dispatch inference<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, configurable TLS/mTLS
        InfGW-->>AsyncProc: Inference response
        AsyncProc->>Redis: Write result to queue<br/>6379/TCP, configurable TLS
        Processor->>Redis: Poll results<br/>6379/TCP, credentials
        Processor->>PG: Update job status<br/>5432/TCP, credentials
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Operator,KubeAPI: Flow 3: Operator Reconciliation
        KubeAPI-->>Operator: Watch event (LLMBatchGateway CR)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, TLS
        Operator->>Operator: Render Helm charts<br/>(batch-gateway + async-processor)
        Operator->>KubeAPI: Server-Side Apply resources<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, ServiceAccount token
        Operator->>KubeAPI: Garbage-collect orphans<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, ServiceAccount token
        Operator->>KubeAPI: Update CR status<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, ServiceAccount token
    end
